</a></div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>The cause:</strong></p>
<p>Typically, this investigation would start with an architecture &amp; design meeting, followed by adding line-by-line logging, adding stop points in our code, and digging into a bunch of other open-ended questions. However, I knew we had&nbsp;<a href="https://github.com/getsentry/seer">Seer</a>&nbsp;(our AI service) instrumented with Sentry Profiling. So naturally, I opened up a profile that one developer had recently run on Autofix, and dug in.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Immediately, the flame graph revealed something totally unexpected. Our&nbsp;<code>from_repo_definition</code> method, which was used to integrate with developers&rsquo; GitHub repositories, was being called over and over again &ndash; multiple times when processing the stack trace, multiple times loading relevant code at the start of the fix step, and once every time Autofix looked at a code file. Even worse, it added over a second of lag each time.<picture><source srcset="https://images.ctfassets.net/em6l9zw4tzag/6yt8NFEFqSZPYeDsUmYYWN/44c703c6f52c8a98414d250afac5a886/profiling_1.png?w=400&amp;h=169&amp;q=50&amp;fm=webp 400w,
